# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CxA Centre of Excellence — environment
#
# Copy to `.env` (never commit it). Names deliberately MIRROR the Field Repository
# backend (backend/app/core/config.py) so the CoE is another tenant of the same
# primitives rather than a parallel stack with its own vocabulary.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Runtime client. Point at the transaction-mode pooler where one exists.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/cxa?schema=public"
# Migrations and any long-lived connection (prisma migrate, seeding). Session mode.
DIRECT_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/cxa?schema=public"

# ── Authentication ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MUST be at least 32 characters of real entropy. `openssl rand -base64 48`.
# The app REFUSES TO START with a short, blank or placeholder secret — a signing
# key that is guessable is indistinguishable from no authentication at all.
JWT_SECRET=""
# Only symmetric HMAC is ever legitimate here. An asymmetric name whose "public
# key" is this shared secret is the classic algorithm-confusion forgery.
JWT_ALGORITHM="HS256"
ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL_MINUTES="30"
REFRESH_TOKEN_TTL_DAYS="30"
# Cookie scope. Leave blank for host-only cookies (the correct default).
AUTH_COOKIE_DOMAIN=""

# ── Object storage (S3-compatible: AWS S3, MinIO, R2, Backblaze) ─────────────
S3_BUCKET="cxa-media"
S3_REGION="ap-south-1"
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=""
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=""
# Set for MinIO / R2 / any non-AWS endpoint. Leave blank for AWS S3 proper.
S3_ENDPOINT=""
# The origin the BROWSER uses for presigned uploads, when it differs from S3_ENDPOINT — a container
# stack where the server says "minio:9000" and the browser says "localhost:9000", or a private VPC
# endpoint behind a public gateway. Leave blank when both reach storage at the same address.
# It cannot be a string replacement after signing: SigV4 covers the Host header.
S3_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT=""
# MinIO and most self-hosted gateways require path-style addressing.
S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE="false"
# Server-side encryption algorithm, e.g. "AES256". Blank disables the header.
S3_SSE_ALGORITHM=""
# Public read base for the bucket, e.g. "https://media.example.org" or
# "http://localhost:9000/cxa-media".
#
# ⚠ READ AT BUILD TIME ONLY, and by one reader: next.config.ts derives the image optimiser's host
# allowlist from it. It is NOT a runtime variable and it CANNOT stand in for NEXT_PUBLIC_CDN_URL —
# nothing signs a URL for an <img>. Signing exists for document downloads
# (app/api/public/files/[slug]) and nowhere else, so leaving the CDN base blank does not fall back to
# a signed URL; it renders every photograph on the site as an "Image unavailable" placeholder.
# lib/env.ts warns about exactly that at boot.
S3_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=""
# How long a soft-deleted asset's BYTES survive before the purge job may remove them. The recycle
# bin is only a real safety net if the object it points at still exists, so keep this generous —
# anything shorter than a working fortnight turns "restore what we deleted before the holidays"
# into a permanent loss.
MEDIA_PURGE_AFTER_DAYS="30"

# ── CDN ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public origin the browser sees for media. Must be in next.config.ts's allowlist
# — it is derived from this value, so setting it here is sufficient.
#
# ⚠ EMPTY IS SAFE BUT IT IS NOT A SERVING CONFIGURATION. Nothing breaks and nothing is requested
# wrongly — mediaSrc() returns null and MediaImage draws a labelled "no CDN configured" placeholder
# rather than an <img src="">, which every browser resolves to the current page and re-downloads the
# whole document as an image. But the placeholder is what a READER sees in place of every photograph,
# and there is no signed-URL fallback to rescue it. Empty is the right value while storage is still
# being set up; it is the wrong value on a site anybody is looking at.
#
# FOR A CORPUS-ONLY DEMO WITH NO OBJECT STORAGE AT ALL, point it at the site's own origin:
#
#     NEXT_PUBLIC_CDN_URL="http://localhost:3000"
#
# The demonstration corpus (npx tsx prisma/seed.ts --with-corpus) writes its MediaAsset rows with
# objectKey "craft/<slug>.jpg", which is exactly where the bundled, openly licensed photographs sit
# under public/ — so with the line above every seeded craft, project and article shows a real
# photograph served by the very server rendering the page, with no S3 or MinIO running at all.
#
# ⚠ AND THAT TRICK STOPS BEING SAFE THE MOMENT S3_* IS SET. It works only because the corpus keys
# happen to name files that exist under public/. Everything an editor UPLOADS is keyed
# "media/YYYY/MM/…" (lib/storage/keys.ts) and lands in the BUCKET, which the Next server has never
# heard of — so the origin resolves every one of them to a 404 and the upload appears to have
# silently failed. Once uploads are configured, this must be the bucket's own public base
# (S3_PUBLIC_BASE_URL's value), not the site's origin.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CDN_URL=""

# ── Site ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Absolute origin. Used for canonical URLs, Open Graph, sitemap.xml and robots.txt.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:3000"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_NAME="Centre of Excellence"

# ── Sign in with Google / Microsoft / Yahoo ─────────────────────────────────
# Each is OPTIONAL and independent. A provider with no client id is not rendered
# on the sign-in page at all — a greyed-out button invites a click that cannot
# succeed. Full setup, including the callback URL to register, is in
# docs/SIGN-IN.md.
#
# ⚠ A PROVIDER ANSWERS "WHO IS THIS?", NEVER "SHOULD THEY BE HERE?". Entry is
# decided by the studio access list (Studio → Studio access), which every
# sign-in path consults before a session is issued or an account created.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""

MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=""
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=""
# Your Entra directory (tenant) ID. Blank means `common`, which accepts ANY
# Microsoft account including personal ones. Naming your tenant is the narrower
# door, and it lets the token issuer be pinned exactly rather than matched by shape.
MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID=""

# ⚠ Yahoo rejects http:// redirect URIs, so local testing needs an HTTPS tunnel.
# Google and Microsoft both accept http://localhost.
YAHOO_CLIENT_ID=""
YAHOO_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# ── Scheduled jobs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared secret for /api/cron/*. Sent as `Authorization: Bearer <secret>`.
# WITHOUT IT THE CRON ENDPOINTS REFUSE EVERY REQUEST — the safe direction: an
# unauthenticated purge endpoint on the public internet is worse than a purge
# that never runs.
CRON_SECRET=""

# ── Seeding (development only) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The seed refuses to create an administrator without these, rather than shipping
# a default credential that would survive into production.
SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL=""
SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=""
SEED_ADMIN_NAME="Centre Administrator"
# Optional. Comma-separated addresses put on the STUDIO ACCESS LIST — the list that
# decides who may sign in at all, by password or by Google/Microsoft/Yahoo. Nobody
# not on it can sign in, and nobody on it gets an account until they actually do.
# The first sign-in creates an ADMINISTRATOR, not a master administrator: the top
# tier is only ever granted to an existing account by an existing master admin, so
# there is a person behind it rather than an environment variable. Existing grants
# are never rewritten, and a revoked one is never reinstated.
SEED_MASTER_ADMIN_EMAILS=""

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CloudConvert — DOCX/PPTX → PDF, converted ONCE AT UPLOAD.
#
# Why a conversion at all: no browser renders Word or PowerPoint, so
# components/sections/DocumentEmbedSection.tsx frames a PDF natively and shows a
# download card for everything else. Normalising to PDF at upload means one
# reader-facing path instead of three, and it reuses the renderer that already
# handles the CSP and sandbox traps documented in that file.
#
# Why at UPLOAD rather than an embedded viewer: Office Online and Google Docs
# Viewer render a deck in an iframe by fetching it from our storage into theirs,
# on every page load, cached indefinitely — including a document withdrawn an
# hour later. Converting once means the third party sees the file a single time,
# from our server, and readers are served a static PDF from our own CDN.
#
# ⚠ ABSENT IS A VALID STATE. With no key the upload succeeds and the document
# keeps its download card, exactly as today. Conversion is an enhancement, never
# a gate on getting a file into the library.
CLOUDCONVERT_API_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MapTiler — the STUDIO's coordinate pickers, and only those.
#
# What it buys: vector tiles and a place SEARCH, so an editor recording a cluster
# in rural Odisha types "Barpali" and the camera goes there, instead of panning
# two thousand kilometres across a map of the whole country. The search moves the
# CAMERA and never sets a value — see lib/geo/placeSearch.ts on why a geocoder's
# guess must not reach a record with nobody in the loop.
#
# ⚠ ABSENT IS A VALID STATE, and a deliberate one. Without a key
# components/studio/fields/MapPointPicker.tsx reports itself unavailable and each
# caller falls back to the hand-drawn India outline in
# components/studio/RegionMapPicker.tsx — which has no search but does draw the
# SIBLING regions, so it is a different trade rather than a lesser one. Nothing
# is broken by leaving this empty; the typed latitude and longitude boxes beside
# every map set the same value and need no network at all.
#
# ⚠ NEXT_PUBLIC_ MEANS IT SHIPS IN THE BROWSER BUNDLE. It cannot be a secret, so
# restrict it by domain in the MapTiler dashboard — that, not concealment, is
# what stops someone else spending the quota.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPTILER_API_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The FALLBACK basemap, for a build with no MapTiler key above.
#
# ⚠ THIS USED TO BE THE PUBLIC MAPS' BASEMAP AND IS NOW ONLY THE FALLBACK. Every
# map on this site that draws geography — the MAP block, the craft archive, and
# the studio's pin pickers — takes MapTiler's vector style when the key above is
# set, decided once in lib/geo/basemap.ts. The old arrangement gave the studio
# MapTiler and the public site OpenStreetMap raster tiles, so an editor placed a
# pin on one map and a reader saw the same place on a different one.
#
# (The hand-drawn India outline is not a basemap and is unaffected: it is SVG
# geometry, and the boundary it draws is the official depiction.)
#
# With no MapTiler key, the maps fall back to this raster source rather than to a
# grey rectangle, and it defaults to OpenStreetMap's own tiles — fine for
# development and low volume, and NOT fine as a production dependency (see OSM's
# tile usage policy). A deployment running without a MapTiler key at real traffic
# must point this at its own tile server or a commercial one, in the {z}/{x}/{y}
# form, and set NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_ATTRIBUTION to match.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_TILE_URL=
